## EDA Summary
- 675 rows, all categorical signal — no meaningful numeric predictors after excluding vote_count/year/matched_roles
- Target range: 2.3–8.5, mean 6.21, std 0.90; baseline RMSE (predict mean) = 0.90
- LightGBM native categorical handling is definitively the best approach found
- Director is #1 feature in all tree models; curated flags add genuine signal
- Film count features hurt (collinear with native categoricals, cause overfitting)
- Feature space appears near ceiling — further gains require ensemble (Phase 3)

## Strategy & Reflections
- BEST: LightGBM native categorical, num_leaves=31, min_child_samples=3, lr=0.05 → RMSE 0.8097
- Native categorical (LightGBM) >> target encoding >> frequency encoding >> genre-only
- Curated binary flags (is_curated_*) add genuine signal in all experiments
- 675 rows is small — models converge fast (~30-55 trees with early stopping), dataset is at feature ceiling
- Phase 3 stacking approach: Ridge meta-learner on diverse OOF predictions from Iters 5,6,8,9
- Diverse OOF predictions available: LightGBM genre-only, XGBoost, Ridge, LightGBM native cat (x2)

## Global Best
- **Score**: 0.8097 (RMSE)
- **Model**: LightGBM native categorical (num_leaves=31, min_child_samples=3)
